    "An invite code's shape and how a typed code is read, on both ends (ST-010; ADR-0009, 'Guessing invite codes').",
    "",
    "The backend's Invites issues codes and looks them up by the hash of the normalised code; the client's",
    "InviteCodes checks a typed code before it is sent and sends it formatted. Each keeps its own copy of the",
    "rules, so this table is the contract: InviteCodeContractTests (backend) and InviteCodesTests (client) run",
    "every case through their own normaliser, shape check and formatter. A change on one side only, such as",
    "Unicode normalisation (NFKC would fold the full-width and superscript cases below), fails one of them.",
    "",
    "normalised: the letters and digits of what was typed, upper-cased, everything else dropped.",
    "wellFormed: today's length or the old one, every character from the alphabet.",
    "formatted: the normalised code in groups of groupLength joined by '-'.",
    "Every code here is made up; none was issued."
